    {"test_id": "DR040", "name": "What is depreciation", "conversation": conv([user_msg("What is depreciation?")]), "golden_response": "Depreciation is an accounting method that allocates the cost of a tangible asset over its useful life. It represents the decline in value of an asset due to use, wear and tear, or obsolescence. Common methods include straight-line depreciation, declining balance, and units of production.", "notes": "Basic accounting concept"},
    {"test_id": "DR041", "name": "What is accrual accounting", "conversation": conv([user_msg("What is accrual accounting?")]), "golden_response": "Accrual accounting is an accounting method where revenues and expenses are recorded when they are earned or incurred, regardless of when cash is actually received or paid. This contrasts with cash accounting, which only records transactions when cash changes hands. Accrual accounting provides a more accurate picture of a company's financial position.", "notes": "Accounting method"},
    {"test_id": "DR042", "name": "What is materiality", "conversation": conv([user_msg("What does materiality mean in accounting?")]), "golden_response": "Materiality in accounting refers to the significance of an item or information in the context of financial statements. Information is considered material if omitting or misstating it could influence the economic decisions of users. Materiality is both quantitative (size of the item) and qualitative (nature of the item).", "notes": "Accounting concept"},
    {"test_id": "DR043", "name": "What is an audit", "conversation": conv([user_msg("What is a financial audit?")]), "golden_response": "A financial audit is an independent examination of an organization's financial statements and related disclosures. Auditors assess whether the financial statements are presented fairly in accordance with the applicable accounting framework (like IFRS or GAAP) and are free from material misstatement. The result is an audit opinion.", "notes": "Basic audit concept"},
    {"test_id": "DR044", "name": "What is consolidation", "conversation": conv([user_msg("What is consolidation in accounting?")]), "golden_response": "Consolidation in accounting is the process of combining the financial statements of a parent company with its subsidiaries to present them as a single economic entity. The consolidated financial statements eliminate intercompany transactions and balances to show the group's overall financial position and performance.", "notes": "Consolidation concept"},
